<title>COLOMBIA: Spanish-Colombian group wins airport concession.</title>
<headline>Spanish-Colombian group wins airport concession.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Spanish-Colombian consortium, headed by the Spanish aviation company Aeropuertos Espanoles y Navegacion Aerea (AENA), has won a 15-year concession to run Barranquilla airport, Colombia's civil aviation authorities said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The consortium, Aeropuertos del Caribe, was the sole bidder, has put up 9.4 billion pesos and is scheduled to begin operating the Caribbean coast airport, about 430 miles (690 km) north of Bogota, in December.</p>
<p>-- Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom + 571 6107544</p>
</text>
